1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,087
Let's read about Matt's unusual daily routine.

2
00:00:04,087 --> 00:00:13,702
I work in London, but flats are expensive there. In Barcelona, they’re nice, big, and not expensive, so I live there!

3
00:00:13,702 --> 00:00:23,156
I fly to London on Monday, work three days, and stay with my sister. Then I fly back to Barcelona and work at home two days.

4
00:00:23,156 --> 00:00:31,541
I study Spanish at a language school on Saturday. I love Barcelona – it’s a beautiful city and great to live here!

5
00:00:31,541 --> 00:00:40,201
Which sentence accurately describes Matt's situation?

6
00:00:40,201 --> 00:00:45,077
The correct answer is: He lives in Barcelona and works in London.

7
00:00:45,077 --> 00:00:53,946
What does Matt say about flats in London and Barcelona?

8
00:00:53,946 --> 00:01:00,784
London flats are expensive, while Barcelona flats are nice, big, and not expensive.

9
00:01:00,784 --> 00:01:11,383
How many days does Matt work in London and at home, and what about his Spanish studies?

10
00:01:11,383 --> 00:01:17,200
He works 3 days in London, 2 days at home, and studies Spanish on Saturday.

11
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:25,709
Finally, what does Matt say about Barcelona?

12
00:01:25,709 --> 00:01:29,226
He says it's a beautiful city and great to live there.

13
00:01:29,226 --> 00:01:33,383
Let's learn about Pablo and Alicia's diverse family.

14
00:01:33,383 --> 00:01:41,222
Pablo from Spain and Alicia from Argentina are married and live in New York. Their family is very international!

15
00:01:41,222 --> 00:01:52,951
Alicia's sister Daniela, who is 46, lives in Buenos Aires with their mother. Her brother Carlos, 37, lives and works in São Paulo, Brazil.

16
00:01:52,951 --> 00:02:05,994
Pablo and Alicia have two children. Their son Alex, 19, is at university in Mexico. Their daughter María, 24, lives in Istanbul with her Turkish husband, Mehmet.

17
00:02:05,994 --> 00:02:13,923
Are Pablo and Alicia's children small?

18
00:02:13,923 --> 00:02:18,929
False. Their children are 19 and 24, not small.

19
00:02:18,929 --> 00:02:30,425
Is María married and living in Turkey? And is it true that only Pablo and Alicia live in Mexico?

20
00:02:30,425 --> 00:02:39,309
María is married and lives in Turkey is true. Only Pablo and Alicia in Mexico is false, as Alex lives there too.

21
00:02:39,309 --> 00:02:50,616
Can you name the countries where Daniela, Carlos, Alex, María, and Mehmet live?

22
00:02:50,616 --> 00:02:58,128
Daniela in Argentina, Carlos in Brazil, Alex in Mexico, and María and Mehmet in Turkey.

23
00:02:58,128 --> 00:03:06,660
What are the ages of Carlos, Alex, and María?

24
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:11,885
Carlos is thirty-seven, Alex is nineteen, and María is twenty-four.

25
00:03:11,885 --> 00:03:15,890
Let's read an email from Maria about her family.

26
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:27,038
Hi Eileen, my family is small. Here’s a new photo of us on holiday with my husband, Greg, our daughter, Linda, and our son, Jeff.

27
00:03:27,038 --> 00:03:34,434
My parents, Tom from San Francisco and Elizabetta from Warsaw, Poland, are in the photo, too.

28
00:03:34,434 --> 00:03:41,147
Greg and I live in Washington with our children. Greg works in an office and I’m a teacher.

29
00:03:41,147 --> 00:03:49,033
Greg’s parents live in Washington, but my mum and dad are in California. We usually have holidays with them.

30
00:03:49,033 --> 00:03:55,572
I have two brothers, Daniel and Jon. Daniel is an English teacher in Mexico City.

31
00:03:55,572 --> 00:04:04,352
Jon lives in Moscow with his Russian wife, Anna, and their five-year-old daughter, Olga. Olga speaks Russian and English well.

32
00:04:04,352 --> 00:04:12,838
Can you match these people to their respective locations?

33
00:04:12,838 --> 00:04:24,378
Daniel in Mexico City, Eileen in Edinburgh, Elizabetta from Warsaw, Greg and Maria in Washington, Jon in Moscow, and Tom from San Francisco.

34
00:04:24,378 --> 00:04:34,036
Who are Maria's immediate family members, and Jon's wife and daughter?

35
00:04:34,036 --> 00:04:43,861
Maria's parents are Tom and Elizabetta, husband Greg, children Linda and Jeff. Jon's wife is Anna, and daughter is Olga.

36
00:04:43,861 --> 00:04:51,016
You've done a great job learning about these families. Keep practicing your English reading skills!
